    {
      "id": 120100,
      "name": "Reckless",
      "username": "Reckless",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/{size}/2467_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-11-05T04:11:21.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"jcubela2\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/f4b2a3/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> jcubela2:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Does the ongoing effect of a card effect only the hero using it, or all heroes?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p><br>Depends on the card.<br><br>Tempest's Otherworldly Resilience only provides DR to him.&nbsp; But Shielding Winds provides every hero with DR from instances of 5+ damage (that's a single instance of damage, so \"5 (type) damage\", not \"five total damage from one source in a turn (1,3,1/2,2,1/3,2/1,1,1,1,1/etc.)\").&nbsp; However, Legacy's Superhuman Durability only reduces damage to him, as it specifies (but it provides more DR!).<br><br>If a card says \"Increase all damage dealt by 1\" then all damage is increased.&nbsp; Villain, hero, and environment; be it from a target, one-shot, or abstract source like \"the environment\".&nbsp; \"Increase damage dealt by villain targets by 1\", however, increases damage dealt by any villain card that has HP (as a target is a card with HP).<br><br>Hope this helps!</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:53:29.178Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
