      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "[quote=\"jcubela2\"]\n\nDoes the ongoing effect of a card effect only the hero using it, or all heroes?\n\n[/quote]\n<br />Depends on the card.<br /><br />Tempest&#39;s Otherworldly Resilience only provides DR to him.&nbsp; But Shielding Winds provides every hero with DR from instances of 5+ damage (that&#39;s a single instance of damage, so &quot;5 (type) damage&quot;, not &quot;five total damage from one source in a turn (1,3,1/2,2,1/3,2/1,1,1,1,1/etc.)&quot;).&nbsp; However, Legacy&#39;s Superhuman Durability only reduces damage to him, as it specifies (but it provides more DR!).<br /><br />If a card says &quot;Increase all damage dealt by 1&quot; then all damage is increased.&nbsp; Villain, hero, and environment; be it from a target, one-shot, or abstract source like &quot;the environment&quot;.&nbsp; &quot;Increase damage dealt by villain targets by 1&quot;, however, increases damage dealt by any villain card that has HP (as a target is a card with HP).<br /><br />Hope this helps!\n",
